        "original_id": "53860c09-45c5-513e-9bd7-5f0b1f7e3e26",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Garth Richardson, Jack Richardson, Ron Griffiths, David \"Dai\" Jenkins, Ham\n- Bands and artists: Badfinger, The Iveys, Daughters of Mara, Jellyfish, Alice Cooper, The Guess Who, Poco, Mudvayne, Rage Against the Machine\n- Albums and songs: I Am Destroyer, Best!, \"No Matter What\"\n- Companies: Virgin Records\n- Places: Swansea, Wales\n\nFacts:\n- In 1961, Ham, Ron Griffiths, and David \"Dai\" Jenkins formed The Iveys in Swansea, Wales.\n- Badfinger evolved from the earlier group The Iveys.\n- Jack Richardson was a Canadian music producer whose credits included Alice Cooper, The Guess Who, Badfinger, and Poco.\n- Garth Richardson is the son of Canadian music producer Jack Richardson.\n- Daughters of Mara's first album, I Am Destroyer, was produced by Garth Richardson, whose credits include Mudvayne and Rage Against the Machine.\n- Daughters of Mara released I Am Destroyer on Virgin Records.\n- On the album Best!, Jellyfish's song \"No Matter What\" is a live cover of a Badfinger song.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ec089bb6-eae5-5de0-9799-b656a9fc3b25",
        "text": "Page: Garth Richardson. Sentence: He is the son of Canadian music producer Jack Richardson (whose credits include Alice Cooper, The Guess Who, Badfinger and Poco).\nPage: Badfinger. Sentence: The band evolved from an earlier group called The Iveys that was formed in 1961 by Ham, Ron Griffiths and David \"Dai\" Jenkins in Swansea, Wales.\nPage: Daughters of Mara. Sentence: Daughters Of Mara's first album, I Am Destroyer, was produced by Garth Richardson (Mudvayne, Rage Against The Machine) and was released on Virgin Records.\nPage: Best! (Jellyfish album). Sentence: The song \"No Matter What\" is a live cover of a Badfinger song.",
